{"name":"Goan King Prawn Balchão","permalink":"goan-king-prawn-balchao","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/GoanKingPrawnBalchao.scala","source":"Gousto","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":[],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Pescatarian","Scales","Spicy","Low Effort","Quick"],"inherited_tags":[],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Red onions","quantity":"2","prep":"finely diced","notes":null},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"3 cloves","prep":"roughly chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Fresh root ginger","quantity":"15g","prep":"peeled and roughly chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Ground coriander","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Ground cumin","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Dried chilli flakes","quantity":"1/2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Cayenne pepper","quantity":"1/2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Tomato paste","quantity":"32g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"King prawns","quantity":"171g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Tamarind paste","quantity":"15g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Cider vinegar","quantity":"30ml","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Sugar","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Baby leaf spinach","quantity":"80g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Basmati rice","quantity":"130g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Vegetable oil","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Water","quantity":"300ml","prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Fry the onion in a wide pan with a generous drizzle of vegetable oil over a medium heat for 10-12 min or until softened.","Rinse the rice and cook in the water for 10-12 minutes.","Add the chopped garlic, ginger, ground coriander, ground cumin, chilli flakes, cayenne pepper and a generous pinch of salt to a pestle & mortar and grind to a smooth paste. Add 2 tbsp vegetable oil and give everything a good mix up.","Once the onion has softened, add the Balchao spice paste and tomato paste to the pan and cook for 4-5 min or until fragrant.","Add the king prawns, tamarind paste, cider vinegar and 1 tsp sugar and cook for 2-3 min or until the prawns are almost cooked through.","Add the baby leaf spinach with 60ml cold water and cook for a further 2-3 min or until the spinach has just wilted and the sauce is thickened to a curry-like consistency.","Serve the Goan prawn Balchao curry over the basmati rice."]}